# {{ .Project }} Desktop

Generated with Prism and DryIoc.

## Build and run

From the generated project root:

```powershell
dotnet restore .\{{ .Project }}.sln
dotnet build .\src\Desktop\{{ .Project }}.Desktop.csproj
dotnet run --project .\src\Desktop\{{ .Project }}.Desktop.csproj
```

For fullstack projects, start the API first in another terminal:

```powershell
dotnet run --project .\src\WebApi\WebApi.csproj --urls http://localhost:5000
```

The generated entity modules use `http://localhost:5000` by default. Set `ASPGENT_API_URL` when the API uses another address:

```powershell
$env:ASPGENT_API_URL = "https://localhost:7001"
dotnet run --project .\src\Desktop\{{ .Project }}.Desktop.csproj
```

{{- if eq .Theme "wpfui" }}
WPF-UI theme is enabled with the `WPF-UI` NuGet package. Theme resources are configured in `App.xaml`, and the shell uses `FluentWindow`, `TitleBar`, `NavigationView`, `AutoSuggestBox` module search, grouped module navigation, Fluent resource brushes, and Prism regions. The shell also calls `SystemThemeWatcher.Watch(this)` so the app theme, accent, and Mica backdrop stay in sync with Windows light/dark settings.

The dashboard is the initial landing page. It includes a Fluent hero banner and responsive cards for generated modules. The left navigation can collapse with its hamburger button, modules are grouped under **Modules**, PascalCase names are displayed as readable labels, and **Settings** is available in the footer. The initial theme is Dark; use the **Toggle theme** button or Settings page to switch between Light and Dark themes at runtime.

Generated entity forms use WPF-UI controls based on property type: `TextBox`, `NumberBox`, `CalendarDatePicker`, `TimePicker`, and `ToggleSwitch`. Lists use a themed `DataGrid` with typed columns, empty-state feedback, validation and success `InfoBar` messages, and Fluent action icons. Deleting a record prompts for confirmation in a Fluent `ContentDialog` (hosted by the shell's `ContentDialogHost`) before removing it.

CRUD keyboard shortcuts are available in each module: `Ctrl+N` (add new) and `F5` (refresh) on the list page; `Ctrl+S` (save) and `Escape` (cancel) on the edit page. Double-click (or press Enter on) a grid row to open its details page, which has Edit and Delete buttons.

Global shell shortcuts are also available: `Alt+Home` returns to the dashboard and `Ctrl+,` opens Settings.
{{- end }}
